# Enroll Device Sheet

::summary
The device enrollment sheet (RULED 08-05), opened by Add Device: ONE sheet, three enrollment paths — the six-digit pair code with expiry countdown, the QR for mobile scan, and the headless/CLI command. Footer explains what the device gets: a device-scoped key revocable anytime; capabilities are off until enabled.
::

::modal[name=enroll-device title="Enroll device" width=360 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=doc state=readonly href=#]
On the new device, install Surfspace and sign in
Then enter this code, or scan the QR from the mobile app
:::

::::code[lang=text]
742-918            (expires in 9:41)
surfspace devices enroll 742-918
::::

:::figure[src=enroll-qr caption="QR alongside for mobile scan"]
:::

:::row[icon=login state=readonly href=#]
What it gets
A device-scoped key you can revoke anytime; capabilities off until you enable them
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. The pair code stays a monospace code block with a copy affordance; the QR stays a figure. The countdown ticking is state layer; an expired code regenerates in place.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
